From fbef83554b621ee1ad7b6089543a1c4b02782750 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Samuel Price <thesamprice@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 00:55:17 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/9] ld: microblaze: don't read other sections' contents when
 relaxing

When relaxation deletes bytes from a code section, the loop over the
object's other sections adjusts relocations against that section.  It
read and cached the contents of every section holding such a
relocation, with bfd_get_section_contents, although for most of them,
debug sections included, only the addend changes.  For a compressed
debug section that call fails, and the link stops:

  unable to get decompressed section .debug_info
  can't relax section: invalid operation

This happens for any -g object assembled with
--compress-debug-sections; the same object uncompressed, or linked
without --relax, is fine.

Read contents only for the relocations whose instruction words are
rewritten (R_MICROBLAZE_32_LO, 32_PCREL_LO, TEXTREL_32_LO and
64_PCREL), and read them with bfd_malloc_and_get_section, which also
handles compressed sections.  The loop is now a switch over the
relocation type, after a single test that the relocation is against
the relaxed section's symbol.

bfd/
	* elf32-microblaze.c (microblaze_get_cached_contents): New.
	(microblaze_elf_relax_section): Use it, and only for relocations
	in instruction words.

ld/
	* testsuite/ld-microblaze/relax-compressed-debug.s: New file.
	* testsuite/ld-microblaze/relax-compressed-debug.d: New test.

Assisted-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 bfd/elf32-microblaze.c                        | 249 +++++++-----------
